.TH HD-REPO-UPDATE 1 "October 2026" "hd-repo" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-repo-update \- add uploaded packages to the hyprdebian package repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-repo-update
.RI [ suite ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-repo-update
adds the packages in the inboxes to the hyprdebian package repository in
.IR /srv/hd-repo ,
then makes the indices of every suite and signs them.
See
.BR hd-repo (7)
for how the repository is set up and used.
.PP
Without arguments, it takes the packages from the inboxes of all suites,
.I /var/lib/hd-repo/inbox/trixie
and
.IR /var/lib/hd-repo/inbox/unstable .
With arguments, only from the inboxes of the suites named,
.B trixie
or
.BR unstable .
The indices of all suites are made and signed again either way.
.PP
Run it as the user
.BR repo ,
without
.BR sudo (8):
the repository and the key belong to that user.
It is usually run over ssh, after uploading the packages with scp:
.PP
.RS
.nf
scp foo_1.0_amd64.deb repo@repo.example:inbox/unstable/
ssh repo@repo.example hd-repo-update
.fi
.RE
.SH OPERATION
.IP 1. 4
Every package in the inboxes is checked first.
A file that is not a package, or a package that is not for amd64 or all,
stops the update, and the repository and the inboxes stay as they were.
.IP 2. 4
When there are packages and
.I /srv/hd-repo
is a ZFS dataset of its own, a snapshot
.IR <dataset>@hd-repo-update-<date>-<time>
is taken, so the update can be undone with
.BR "zfs rollback" .
When the snapshot fails, the update stops before it changes anything.
.IP 3. 4
Each package is moved from its inbox to the pool of its suite,
.IR /srv/hd-repo/pool/<suite>/main .
Older versions of the same package in that pool are removed.
.IP 4. 4
For every suite, the
.I Packages
index is made with
.BR apt-ftparchive (1),
then the
.I Release
file with its hashes, which is signed into
.I InRelease
and
.IR Release.gpg .
They are made in a temporary directory and moved into place together, so
clients never see indices without the signed Release that matches them.
.IP 5. 4
The public key is exported to
.IR /srv/hd-repo/hyprdebian-archive-keyring.pgp .
.PP
Without new packages, nothing is snapshotted or moved; the repository is
only signed again.
Only one
.B hd-repo-update
runs at a time; a second one stops with an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I suite
Take packages only from the inbox of this suite:
.B trixie
or
.BR unstable .
May be given more than once.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the repository was updated and signed, 1 when the update stopped on an
error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-repo/inbox/<suite>
The inboxes, emptied by a successful update.
.TP
.I /srv/hd-repo
The repository.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/hd-repo/gnupg
The signing key.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-repo/update.lock
Keeps two updates from running at the same time.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add the packages uploaded for both suites:
.PP
.RS
hd-repo-update
.RE
.PP
Add only the packages uploaded for unstable:
.PP
.RS
hd-repo-update unstable
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-repo (7),
.BR apt-ftparchive (1),
.BR gpg (1),
.BR zfs-snapshot (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
